---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Accessibility" description="How this site is built to be usable by everyone, what has been tested, and how to report a barrier." eyebrow="About" lede="The site is built to be read by anyone, on any device, with or without assistive technology." reviewed="2026-11-20" toc={false}>
  <h2 id="built-in">What is built in</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Structure.</strong> Every page has one main heading, ordered subheadings, landmark regions and a link to skip to the content.</li>
    <li><strong>Keyboard.</strong> Everything can be reached and operated from the keyboard, with a visible focus outline.</li>
    <li><strong>Meaning without color.</strong> Reliability grades and evidence states are carried by text labels and shapes. No information depends on color alone.</li>
    <li><strong>Contrast.</strong> Body text meets a contrast ratio of at least 7 to 1 in both light and dark appearance.</li>
    <li><strong>Reflow.</strong> Pages work at phone width without sideways scrolling. Wide tables turn into stacked cards with each value labeled.</li>
    <li><strong>Citations.</strong> Each citation link announces the source it points to and its grade, and each reference links back to where it was cited.</li>
    <li><strong>Motion.</strong> There is no animation. Smooth scrolling is turned off when your system asks for reduced motion.</li>
    <li><strong>Without JavaScript.</strong> All content is readable with scripts turned off. Scripts add only the timeline filter, the glossary filter and search.</li>
    <li><strong>Print.</strong> Pages print cleanly, with the address of each source written out in the reference list.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="tested">What has been tested</h2>
  <p>
    Automated checks run on every build: one main heading per page, unique element identifiers, working internal
    links and anchors, text alternatives, no sideways scrolling at phone width, and readable contrast. Automated
    checks do not catch everything. The site has not yet had an independent audit or testing with screen-reader
    users, and it does not claim formal conformance with a published standard.
  </p>

  <h2 id="known-limits">Known limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Linked source documents are published by others. Many are scanned PDFs that are hard to read with assistive technology.</li>
    <li>Long tables on the claim ledger are dense. The same data is offered as a download for use in your own tools.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="report">Report a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If something on this site is hard to use, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.correctionsEmail}`}>{site.correctionsEmail}</a> with the page and what happened. Barriers
    are treated like errors: fixed, and recorded in the <a href="/updates/">update log</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
